Finding: {"title":"migration-manifest.ts is stale and silently desyncs from the journal on every migration-only commit — feeds a Sentry health check that will false-fire","severity":"HIGH","area":"data-layer / operational monitoring","files":["src/generated/migration-manifest.ts","scripts/generate-migration-manifest.js","src/lib/db-health.ts","package.json"],"detail":"src/generated/migration-manifest.ts is a committed, hand-frozen snapshot (MIGRATION_COUNT = 416, LATEST_MIGRATION = '0424_rate_null_subject_uniqueness') generated by scripts/generate-migration-manifest.js. That script is wired ONLY to `prebuild` (package.json:11), which runs during `npm run build`, not during migration-only commits or via any pre-push/CI gate. The journal (drizzle/meta/_journal.json) currently has 418 entries with the true latest tag `0426_register_atp_frc_analytics_v2_flags` — the manifest is stale by 2 entries and 2 tags behind right now. src/lib/db-health.ts:21 does an exact-equality check `appliedCount !== MIGRATION_COUNT` and fires `Sentry.captureMessage(..., 'error')` on any mismatch. Nothing forces the manifest to be regenerated+committed alongside a migration PR, so it drifts on essentially every migration-adding PR that doesn't happen to run a full `npm run build` before commit. The 'expected' count is also environment-dependent in a way a single hardcoded constant can never represent: several journal tags are stub/orphan entries (0036__pre_push_check, 0050__pre_push_check, 0057__pre_push_check, 0067__pre_push_check) whose SQL files may or may not exist per environment (db-migrate.ts skips tracking them if the file is missing).","impact":"Either Sentry fires a false 'error' on every deploy purely because the manifest wasn't rebuilt after the last migration PR (alert fatigue, real signal ignored), or the frozen count coincidentally matches a broken DB state and a genuine missing-migration incident goes unreported. Either way the check defeats its stated purpose of ops visibility into migration drift.","recommendation":"Either (1) stop comparing to a static frozen number — compute expected count directly from drizzle/meta/_journal.json at runtime, or (2) add a CI/pre-push step that regenerates the manifest and fails if `git diff --exit-code src/generated/migration-manifest.ts` is non-clean, matching the existing schema-drift/orphan-migration/orphan-snapshot pattern already in .husky/pre-push. No such check currently exists for this file.","confidence":"high"}
